---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Related from "../../components/Related.astro";

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  headline: "Dave the Diver Beginner Roadmap",
  description: "Dave the Diver beginner guide: what to upgrade first, how to run the restaurant and which early fish matter.",
  mainEntityOfPage: Astro.url,
};
---

<Base
  title="Dave the Diver Beginner Roadmap - DiverDB"
  description="Dave the Diver beginner guide: what to upgrade first, how to run the restaurant and which early fish matter."
  schema={articleSchema}
>
  <h1>Dave the Diver Beginner Roadmap</h1>

  <div class="toc">
    <strong>In this guide</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>First dives and the money loop</li>
      <li>Restaurant upgrades</li>
      <li>Dive gear priority</li>
      <li>What to keep</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>First dives and the money loop</h2>
  <p>
    The core loop is simple: dive, catch fish and ingredients, then serve them at Bancho Sushi
    at night. Early on, spend the dive budget on a full tank of fish you can already use in a
    recipe instead of chasing the rarest catch. Selling through the daily menu builds the gold
    that unlocks better weapons, restaurant equipment and more dive time.
  </p>
  <p>
    Keep the fish that appear in multiple recipes. High-volume shallow fish are the backbone of
    the first restaurant ranks because they keep the menu full while you learn boss fights and
    VIP requests.
  </p>

  <h2>Restaurant upgrades</h2>
  <p>
    Upgrade in this rough order: more cooking flames, one extra serving slot, then kitchen
    facilities that reduce prep time. Taste upgrades earn better nightly ratings, while extra
    dish capacity is what turns a good menu into a high-gold menu.
  </p>

  <h2>Dive gear priority</h2>
  <p>
    The dive knife is the first reliable weapon, but the net gun is the real early game force
    multiplier. Nets catch live fish for the farm and let you collect more fish per minute than
    killing them. Upgrade oxygen and carry capacity whenever you hit a wall where you run out of
    air before finding the fish you came for.
  </p>

  <h2>What to keep</h2>
  <p>
    Use the <a href="/tools/fish-farm/">Fish Farm Planner</a> to find species with high meat per day.
    For the restaurant, prioritize ingredients that appear in upgraded recipes with high max taste.
    Do not fill the farm with rare one-off catches; use it for steady producers that feed the menu
    every day.
  </p>

  <Related
    heading="Next steps"
    links={[
    { href: "/rankings/", title: "Rankings", sub: "Best fish, dishes, staff and weapons ranked", tool: true },
    { href: "/tools/", title: "Tools", sub: "Planner, filter and compare utilities", tool: true },
  ]}
  />
</Base>
